From 074c3c3dee3014a8fb1150031aef50d738167682 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:18:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/30] Windows ARM64: build with llvm-mingw; LAYA_DEBUG trace;
 laya-probe; live run-tests.bat

The Zig-built ARM64 DLL hung on real Windows on ARM in the first call that throws
inside the library (cause not identified; the same code passes under ARM64 Wine).
- scripts/capi/build-arm64.sh: Windows target now uses llvm-mingw (LLVM_MINGW=...)
- cmake/toolchains/llvm-mingw-aarch64.cmake
- LAYA_DEBUG=1: entry-point and model-load progress on stderr
- tests/capi/probe.cpp: stand-alone C++ runtime probe (laya-probe)
- run-tests.bat prints live instead of collecting a log file
- test-capi announces the contract steps and the model load

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LAsYHSSgSysMFa8MKPJWgL
